ADOPTING ORDIANCE
ORDINANCE 04-10
AN ORDINANCE TO ADOPT SUPPLEMENT 2004 S-1 TO THE TOWN OF ELLETTSVILLE, INDIANA
CODE OF ORDINANCES
   WHEREAS, American Legal Publishing Corporation of Cincinnati, Ohio, has
completed the 2004 S-1 Supplement to the Code of Ordinances of the Political
Subdivision, which supplement contains all ordinance of a general and permanent
nature enacted since the prior supplement to the Code of Ordinance of the
Political Subdivision; and
   WHEREAS, American Legal Publishing Corporation has recommended the revision
or addition of certain sections of the Code of Ordinance which are based on or
make reference to sections of the Indiana Code; and
   WHEREAS, it is the intent of the Ellettsville Town Council to accept these
updated section in accordance with the changes of the law of the State of
Indiana; and
   WHEREAS, it is necessary to provide for the usual daily operation of the
municipality and for the immediate preservation of public peace, health, safety
and general welfare of the municipality that this ordinance take effect at an
early date.
   NOW, THEREFORE BE IT ORDAINED BY THE TOWN COUNCIL OF ELLETTSVILLE, INDIANA:
   SECTION 1. That the 2004 S-1 Supplement to the Code of Ordinances of the
Town of Ellettsville as submitted by American Legal Publishing Corporation of
Cincinnati, Ohio, and as attached hereto, be and the same is hereby adopted by
reference as if set out in its entirety.
   SECTION 2. Such supplement shall be deemed published as of the day of its
adoption and approval by the Ellettsville Town Council and Ellettsville Clerk-
Treasurer is hereby authorized and ordered to insert such supplement into the
copy of the Code of Ordinances kept on file in the Office of the Clerk-
Treasurer.
   SECTION 4. This ordinance is declared to be an emergency measure necessary
for the immediate preservation of the peace, health, safety and general welfare
of the people of this municipality, and shall take effect at the earliest date
provided by law.
   This ordinance takes effect upon passage. This ordinance was passed and
adopted by the Town Council of Ellettsville, Indiana at the Ellettsville Town
Hall on the 28th day of June 2004.
Attest:
ELLETTSVILLE TOWN COUNCIL
Sandra C. Hash /s/
Sandra Hash,                                 Patrick Stoffers /s/  
Clerk-Treasurer                              Patrick Stoffers, President
