GENERAL PROVISIONS
§ 32.01 VOTER QUALIFICATIONS.
   In accordance with state law, any individual who wishes to cast a ballot in
either a primary or a general election for town officials must be a resident of
the town and a registered voter of the town pursuant to the provisions of
applicable state law. If an individual does not qualify in accordance with the
applicable statutes, he or she shall not be entitled to vote in either the
primary or the general election for town officials.
(1985 Code, § 292-5) (Ord. 82-3, passed 12-20-1982)
ELECTION OF OFFICERS
§ 32.15 COUNCIL MEMBERS; ELECTION BY VOTERS OF WHOLE TOWN.
   The members of the Council shall be elected by the voters of the whole town.
The district candidate in each ward receiving the most votes from the votes
cast in the whole town is elected to the Council.
(1985 Code, § 295-5) (Am. Ord. 86-18, passed 11-3-1986)
§ 32.16 COUNCIL MEMBERS; ELIGIBILITY.
   (A)   A person is eligible to be a district member of the Town Council if he
or she:
      (1)   Is a resident of the ward from which he or she seeks election;
      (2)   Has established residency in the ward at least one year prior to
the date upon which he or she would take office, if elected;
      (3)   Is a registered voter of the town; and
      (4)   Has been properly certified as a candidate by the Clerk of the
Circuit Court.
   (B)   All candidates for election as a member of the Town Council must be
properly qualified and certified in accordance with state law.
(1985 Code, § 295-10) (Ord. 82-3, passed 12-20-1982; Am. Ord. 86-18, passed 11-
3-1986)
§ 32.17 CLERK-TREASURER; ELECTION BY WHOLE TOWN.
   The Clerk-Treasurer of the town shall be elected by the voters of the whole
town.
(1985 Code, § 297-5) (Ord. 82-3, passed 12-20-1982)
§ 32.18 CLERK-TREASURER; ELIGIBILITY.
   (A)   A person is eligible to be Clerk-Treasurer of the town if he or she:
      (1)   Is a resident of the town;
      (2)   Has been a resident of the town for a period of one year prior to
the date upon which he or she would assume office if elected;
      (3)   Is a registered voter of the town; and
      (4)   Has been duly certified as a candidate by the Clerk of the Circuit
Court.
   (B)   All candidates for election to the office of Clerk-Treasurer must be
properly qualified and certified in accordance with state law.
(1985 Code, § 297-10) (Ord. 82-3, passed 12-20-1982)
ELECTION DISTRICTS
§ 32.30 DIVISION INTO WARDS.
   The town shall be divided into election districts called wards for the
purpose of conducting elections of officers of the town in accordance with the
laws and procedures for the election of town officials. The wards must be
composed of contiguous territory, be reasonably compact, and contain, as nearly
as possible, equal population.
(1985 Code, § 290-5) (Ord. 194, passed 12-16-1974; Am. Ord. 2022-09, passed 9-
12-2022)
§ 32.31 DIVISION EVERY TEN YEARS.
   Division of the town into wards shall be made by the Town Council in 2002
and every ten years after 2002. A division may also be made in any other year
in the discretion of the Town Council.
(1985 Code, § 290-10) (Am. Ord. 01-33, passed 1-14-2002)
§ 32.32 WARD BOUNDARIES.
   (A)   Five wards are created: Ward 1, Ward 2, Ward 3, Ward 4 and Ward 5.
Each of these wards is comprised of numbered census blocks as set forth below.
