§ 35.01 ESTABLISHMENT.
   The Town Police Alliance is hereby created to assist the Town Police
Department as determined necessary by the Town Marshal.
(1985 Code, § 298-5) (Ord. 91-24, passed 11-25-1991; Am. Ord. 2018-27, passed
9-10-2018)
§ 35.02 APPOINTMENT.
   Police Alliance members for certification shall be appointed by the Town
Council.
(1985 Code, § 298-10) (Ord. 91-24, passed 11-25-1991; Am. Ord. 2018-27, passed
9-10-2018)
§ 35.03 AUTHORITY.
   Police Alliance members may not be members of the regular Police Department
but they shall have all the same police powers as regular members except as
limited by the rules of the Department. The Department shall adopt rules to
limit the authority of Police Alliance members.
(1985 Code, § 298-15) (Ord. 91-24, passed 11-25-1991; Am. Ord. 2018-27, passed
9-10-2018)
§ 35.04 COMPENSATION.
   Upon proper appropriation the Police Alliance members may:
   (A)   Be provided with uniforms, which uniforms shall remain the property of
the town; and
   (B)   Be insured for accident coverage.
(1985 Code, § 298-20) (Ord. 91-24, passed 11-25-1991; Am. Ord. 07-11, passed
11-13-2007; Am. Ord. 2018-27, passed 9-10-2018)
§ 35.05 INELIGIBILITY FOR PENSIONS.
   Police Alliance members are not eligible to participate in any pension
program provided for regular members of the Department.
(1985 Code, § 298-25) (Ord. 91-24, passed 11-25-1991; Am. Ord. 2018-27, passed
9-10-2018)
§ 35.06 TRAINING.
   (A)   (1)   Police Alliance members must, within six months of appointment,
successfully complete training in the following subjects: criminal and traffic
law, firearms, and cuffing, baton, and defensive tactics.
      (2)   The Town Marshal may, at his or her discretion, establish
additional training requirements, provided those requirements are applied
uniformly.
   (B)   A Police Alliance member shall not carry a sidearm until he or she has
successfully completed training in firearms and has qualified on the firing
range under supervision of a certified firearms instructor.
(1985 Code, § 295-26) (Ord. 91-24, passed 11-25-1991; Am. Ord. 91-27, passed 1-
13-1991; Am. Ord. 2018-27, passed 9-10-2018)
Penalty, see § 10.99
§ 35.07 PROBATION.
   Police Alliance members shall be on probation for a period of six months
from the date they become qualified to function as a Police Alliance member.
(1985 Code, § 298-30) (Ord. 91-24, passed 11-25-1991; Am. Ord. 2018-27, passed
9-10- 2018)
§ 35.08 MINIMUM PARTICIPATION REQUIREMENT.
   Police Alliance members will be required to work a minimum of 16 hours per
month for the town.
(1985 Code, § 298-35) (Ord. 91-24, passed 11-25-1991; Am. Ord. 92-23, passed
10-12-1992; Am. Ord. 2018-27, passed 9-10-2018)
§ 35.09 DISCIPLINE.
   Police Alliance members are not paid police officers and therefore, are not
entitled to the same rights and procedures that are available to paid police
officers. The Town Marshal has the absolute discretion to suspend, dismiss, or
otherwise discipline a Police Alliance member.
(1985 Code, § 298-36) (Ord. 97-01, passed 1-10-1997; Am. Ord. 2018-27, passed
9-10-2018)
